Description: Keep AltGr held while a Ctrl+Alt layer is held (Belgian AZERTY project patch)
 What: when a key in a layer such as [control+alt] sends a key with other
 modifiers (for example Ctrl+Alt+2 -> AltGr+2 on a Belgian layout), keyd
 normally puts the layer's own modifiers (Ctrl and Alt) back down on the
 key's release, and takes them off again on the next press. With this patch,
 keyd leaves the sent modifiers (AltGr) down while every layer that produced
 the key is still held. The next key press, or the layer's release, sets the
 right modifiers anyway, because update_mods() runs on every press and on
 every layer change.
 .
 Why: Ctrl+Alt+2 E 2 E then reaches the desktop as AltGr down, 2, E, 2, E
 (2 events per character) instead of about 8 events per character. On Ubuntu
 24.04 based desktops the ibus input method can reorder fast key events
 (see ibus issue #2934); fewer modifier events leave less room for that.
 .
 Measured (QEMU/KVM, keys 30 ms apart and overlapping, original and patched
 keyd alternating, 4 rounds of 50 lines each, lines with swapped characters):
   Linux Mint 22.3 (Cinnamon, X11):  Ctrl+Alt 88/200 -> 8/200; AltGr 11 and 9
   Zorin OS 18.1 (GNOME, Wayland):   Ctrl+Alt 37/200 -> 23/200; AltGr 18 and 20
 Ctrl+Alt+T and Ctrl+Alt+Left/Right still worked right after a symbol
 (Zorin, measured build): keyd puts Ctrl+Alt back down on that key's press.
 .
 Test suite: six t/*.t expectations are updated here, nothing is skipped.
 swap, swap2, swap3, swap4 and swap8 expected Shift to be released and
 pressed again between two shifted keys; it now stays down (same text).
 composite expected Ctrl to be released before Alt when the layer ends; Alt
 now goes first (no text either way). With these, make test-io passes 86/86.
 .
 The code is byte-identical to the build that was measured
 (research/keyd-hold-altgr-test.patch), which is why its comments still say
 "test patch".
 .
 Not covered: pressing Ctrl+Alt again for every symbol (nothing changes
 there); a mouse click with Ctrl+Alt right after a symbol sees AltGr until
 the next key press (untested); real hardware.
Author: Belgian AZERTY for Linux maintainers <linuxbelgiumkeyboard.rc0g4@aleeas.com>
Forwarded: no (a proposal for keyd upstream, https://github.com/rvaiya/keyd; not
 sent yet). Shipped in this project's keyd build of 0.9.4-0.9.7 only; from 0.9.8
 the project uses the keyd-team PPA's unpatched keyd and keeps this file only as
 the proposal.
Last-Update: 2026-10-25
